you don’t like the way you sound on-camera, start humming along to the top creators. then hum along to some of your existing videos. you’ll probably noticed that there’s no rhythm or the pacing is monotonous. the more you do this, the more you can pick up on patterns you can add to your delivery. also, put in the reps… obviously. 

@higherupwellness & @justinescameraroll_ are in the top 1% of on-camera communicators. it’s largely because of the reps and the fact they care about what they’re saying. but they have a signature way of delivering their message that almost acts like a hook itself. chatgbt can now make the perfect script, but what sets you apart from everyone else are the things that make you human. 

#contentcreator

Nobody compliments a layout. But everyone feels it when it’s wrong, and your layout gets judged before a single word gets 
read. 

Land-book curates landing pages you can filter down to a single component, so one pricing block can be studied twenty different ways. 

@godlywebsite keeps a high floor on landing pages specifically. 

@siteinspire has been running since 2009 and its archives show how typography and grid systems have moved over the years. 

@awwwards is for ambition rather than patterns, since the winners chase spectacle. 

@mobbindesign documents real app flows screen by screen, which teaches hierarchy better than most courses on it.

